{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":17,"start_col":10,"end_line":17,"end_col":20,"message":"`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileWrite` here. The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileWrite` does not raise it.\nhelp: add a `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` parameter to `main` (e.g. `fn main(…, _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite))`), or widen the whole grant to `Cap(IO)`, or remove the use.","code":"cap_grant_exceeded","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":23,"start_col":31,"end_line":23,"end_col":31,"text":", _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite)"},"labels":[{"file":"errors/cap_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":24,"start_col":4,"end_line":24,"end_col":9,"message":"`main` calls `greet` here"},{"file":"errors/cap_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":23,"start_col":2,"end_line":25,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` here"}],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
